{"claim_id": "S16-01", "task_id": "S16-STEP1", "claim": "vdPS section 3.2 p.2637, read from the page image: for a differential module of type (0,0,1) the STRONG Riemann-Hilbert problem has a positive answer; the module is represented by d/dz + A_0/z + A_1/(z-1) + A_inf with trace-0 constant matrices, A_inf normalised to (t/2)diag(-1,1) with t in C*, -theta_i^2/4 = det A_i, and the singular points normalised to 0, 1, infinity. NO semisimplicity and NO non-resonance hypothesis is imposed anywhere in this definition.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "render_pages.py", "output_hash": "07356a233e946cb2a78678950aab34383fa02716391a2de3ad545fb3fa0ae8c3", "review": "self", "review_note": "read by viewing the rendered page alone in one message, per the P0 image rule."}
{"claim_id": "S16-02", "task_id": "S16-STEP1", "claim": "vdPS p.2636, read from the page image, defines resonance as a difference of eigenvalues lying in Z\\{0}, and presents resonance and reducibility as sources of SINGULARITIES of the monodromy space R. Such modules are therefore inside the moduli space, not excluded from it. This is the hypothesis the operator flagged as at risk; it is not a hypothesis of this framework.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "render_pages.py", "output_hash": "56194f2639b0aa20d6e96863373e92ee599165e357b6b4b8c9221474b070da6b", "review": "self", "review_note": "p.2636 rendered and viewed; quoted definition only, no interpretation added here."}
{"claim_id": "S16-03", "task_id": "S16-STEP1", "claim": "Packet task 1(b) IS stated in the required form, so the halt condition did not fire. vdPS p.2656, verbatim from the page image: 'the foliation given by the 2-form Omega = dp^dq/(q(q-1)) - dH_V ^ dt on U_0 x (C\\{0}) coincides with the foliation given by isomonodromy.' The flow is (4.4) dp/dt = q(q-1) dH_V/dq, dq/dt = -q(q-1) dH_V/dp with H_V given by (4.5). The operator's description of the framework from memory is CONFIRMED against the text.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "render_pages.py", "output_hash": "fb09f759647ed28244ac5055be85b9899d72a41fff526cca8900ec583fd5eaef", "review": "self", "review_note": "H_V and (4.4) cropped at 6x and viewed alone; transcribed by looking, not by OCR."}
{"claim_id": "S16-04", "task_id": "S16-STEP1", "claim": "The time variable t of vdPS's (0,0,1) family is the SCALE OF THE IRREGULAR TYPE AT INFINITY (A_inf = (t/2)diag(-1,1)), not the position of a singular point. The three singular points are normalised to 0, 1, infinity. This is why an object of this type carries a fixed t with no deformation written down: t is an invariant computed from the configuration, exactly as the operator surmised.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "render_pages.py", "output_hash": "07356a233e946cb2a78678950aab34383fa02716391a2de3ad545fb3fa0ae8c3", "review": "self", "review_note": "reading of the normalisation in section 3.2; structural, not a quotation."}
{"claim_id": "S16-05", "task_id": "S16-STEP1", "claim": "SUSPECTED TYPO IN THE PUBLISHED PAPER, vdPS p.2655, entry b(z) of the family (4.1): the first term prints (p + (1/2)(q-1)q)^2, with no t, while the second term carries (q-1)q t. Tested against the paper's OWN constraint det A(1) = -theta_1^2/4: the printed form leaves a nonzero remainder, whereas (p + (1/2)(q-1)q t)^2 satisfies it IDENTICALLY. det A(0) = -theta_0^2/4 holds for both readings and so does not discriminate. The corrected reading is used for computation and is flagged here rather than adopted silently.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": 0, "reproducible": true, "script": "check_bz.py", "output_hash": "9d2b98b83bae288bac8554ba60f651b3cef8cea5d823c55d633a68cc3d910807", "review": "self", "review_note": "discriminated by an exact symbolic residual, not by preference."}
{"claim_id": "S16-06", "task_id": "S16-STEP2A", "claim": "System C (3x^2+x+1)W'' + (6x+1)W' - x^2 W = 0 has projective normal potential r_C(x) = (12x^4+4x^3+4x^2+11)/(4(3x^2+x+1)^2); singular points s_pm = (-1 +/- i sqrt(11))/6 with delta = s_- - s_+ = -i sqrt(11)/3. Under x = s_+ + delta z the potential has poles ONLY at z = 0 and z = 1, both double, with coefficient -1/4 at each, and NO apparent singularity. So C's three singular points are exactly vdPS's 0, 1, infinity after the normalising Moebius map.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": 60, "reproducible": true, "script": "systemC_invariants.py", "output_hash": "6d3363083f2a5063b98c95d0fa48ebf9d6e720af9510b9e2d4c4b0f80555a803", "review": "self", "review_note": "exact symbolic derivation; cross-checked numerically at dps 60, worst |diff| 1.1668e-61."}
{"claim_id": "S16-07", "task_id": "S16-STEP2C", "claim": "H-c SATISFIED, exactly. At infinity r_z = -11/27 + (i sqrt(11)/27)/z + ..., and vdPS's normalisation gives t^2/4 = R(infinity), hence t = -/+ 2 i sqrt(33)/9. This is EXACTLY the value the companion v1.2 prints for System C. The companion's t is therefore vdPS's time invariant, computed from the configuration, and there is no mismatch to explain.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "systemC_invariants.py", "output_hash": "6d3363083f2a5063b98c95d0fa48ebf9d6e720af9510b9e2d4c4b0f80555a803", "review": "self", "review_note": "symbolic; the match is to an exact algebraic number, not a numerical agreement."}
{"claim_id": "S16-08", "task_id": "S16-STEP2A", "claim": "Dictionary between vdPS's family (4.1) and the projective normal potential, established by probing three EXACT draws: double-pole coefficient at z=0 is (theta_0^2-1)/4 (3/3), at z=1 is (theta_1^2-1)/4 (3/3), and R(infinity) = t^2/4 (3/3). The naive 1/z entry t*theta_inf/2 FAILED all three; the data give t(theta_inf+1)/2, the +1 being the scalar-reduction shift. The failure is reported because it is the reason the located theta_inf is -2 -/+ sqrt(3)/9 and not -1 -/+ sqrt(3)/9.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": 0, "reproducible": true, "script": "probe_family.py", "output_hash": "c64115bb0c515c3210363b946278a6f9aa34f8eb742f56c71868d30e6f954da7", "review": "self", "review_note": "three exact draws carrying theta_0 != 0; these draws are also the H-a vacuity control, since the observable does report a nonzero theta_0."}
{"claim_id": "S16-09", "task_id": "S16-STEP2A", "claim": "H-a SATISFIED, AGAINST PRE-REGISTRATION. PREREG.md recorded the expectation that H-a would be VIOLATED or UNDECIDED. System C has theta_0 = theta_1 = 0, so det A_i = 0 and tr A_i = 0 and A_0, A_1 are NILPOTENT and nonzero (c(0) = q/(q-1) != 0 on U_0, and C1 forces a log term): non-semisimple local data. But the eigenvalue difference is 0, which is NOT in Z\\{0}, so the data are not resonant in vdPS's sense; and section 3.2 imposes no semisimplicity condition in any case. The operator's worry that resonance might violate a hypothesis does NOT materialise in this framework. vdPS admit precisely the logarithmic local data that Jimbo's (A1) excludes.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "probe_family.py", "output_hash": "c64115bb0c515c3210363b946278a6f9aa34f8eb742f56c71868d30e6f954da7", "review": "self", "review_note": "rests on the ABSENCE of a hypothesis in the source, which is why it is STRUCTURAL and not PROVEN; the reading is claim S16-01."}
{"claim_id": "S16-10", "task_id": "S16-STEP2B", "claim": "H-b SATISFIED: System C is IRREDUCIBLE over C(x), proven exactly. Riccati test w' + w^2 = r: any solution has only simple poles; residues at s_pm satisfy A^2 - A = -1/4 so A = 1/2; w is bounded at infinity with c_0^2 = 1/3; matching the 1/x coefficient r_1 = -1/9 forces n = r_1/(2c_0) - 1 = -1 -/+ sqrt(3)/18, irrational and hence not a non-negative integer. Contradiction. So C does NOT sit on the classical Riccati locus.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "irreducibility2.py", "output_hash": "dac25adcc2f5d017d7ee6382ed3245160917a55987f3566fb80bd47795002411", "review": "self", "review_note": "exact; both controls are assertions - a reducible-by-construction operator is returned REDUCIBLE and an irreducible one IRREDUCIBLE."}
{"claim_id": "S16-11", "task_id": "S16-METHOD", "claim": "DEFECT CAUGHT AND RECORDED: the first irreducibility script was VOID. sp.cancel((x-c)**2 * r).subs(x, c) returns nan for algebraic c, so the admissible-residue list came out empty, the product over it was empty, and the verdict IRREDUCIBLE was reached WITH NO TEST PERFORMED. It was caught only by the reducible-by-construction control, which was also declared irreducible. Related: all(m == 2 for m in sp.roots(...).values()) is vacuously True on an empty dict. General lesson: a step that cannot fail cannot be trusted to report failure; every control must be an assertion. irreducibility.py is retained as the record.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "irreducibility.py", "output_hash": "c34010320b50e23db7f7e0ca3af53259b5d34bbaa0839da51801accf828af1c0", "review": "self", "review_note": "the defect is demonstrated by the retained void script and its output."}
{"claim_id": "S16-12", "task_id": "S16-STEP3A", "claim": "STEP 3(a) COMPLETE. System C's projective normal form coincides with that of vdPS's family (4.1) at an explicit point of the chart U_0 = C x (C\\{0,1}) of M_{t,lambda}, for both sign branches. Branch t = -2i sqrt(33)/9: theta_inf = -2 - sqrt(3)/9, q = 1/2 + i(-457937 sqrt(11) + 281700 sqrt(33))/122408 ~ 0.5 + 0.8123 i, p = 5i(-28151758571 sqrt(33) + 48874838016 sqrt(11))/4086468672 ~ 0.4649 i. Branch t = +2i sqrt(33)/9: theta_inf = -2 + sqrt(3)/9, q ~ 0.5 - 25.6278 i, p ~ 396.2089 i. The solve was OVERDETERMINED - five coefficient equations plus b_1 = 0 in four unknowns - and consistent.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": 60, "reproducible": true, "script": "locate_final.py", "output_hash": "3b3e63d3c397ea8cadabff5aed4537b7e2bd1baf888ea5a3d8c2f3127d39e1f0", "review": "self", "review_note": "located by a hand-reduced closed form; see S16-13 for the independent check."}
{"claim_id": "S16-13", "task_id": "S16-STEP3A", "claim": "INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION of S16-12: re-substituting each solution into the GENERAL formula for R - not the reduced closed form used to derive it - gives R - r_z simplifying identically to 0, with worst relative residual over five points at dps 60 of 5.79877e-56 (branch 1) and 7.00553e-61 (branch 2); b_1 = 0 in both; and q not in {0,1} in both, so the point lies in the chart U_0.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": 60, "reproducible": true, "script": "verify_point.py", "output_hash": "be1e05416c1c2c566d8514d9237d1fffeffaae0c644ae32d7126dee35eae3539", "review": "self", "review_note": "re-derivation by a different route from the one that produced the value; still self, since the same agent wrote both."}
{"claim_id": "S16-14", "task_id": "S16-MEMBERSHIP", "claim": "MEMBERSHIP, the packet's question. System C satisfies every hypothesis under which vdPS build the moduli space M for the (0,0,1) row: H-a SATISFIED (S16-09), H-b SATISFIED (S16-10), H-c SATISFIED (S16-07). It is a point of the chart U_0 (S16-12, S16-13). Since PV IS the isomonodromy foliation on that space (S16-03), and since q(q-1) != 0 and t != 0 at the point so the vector field (4.4) is regular there, exactly one PV leaf passes through System C. The deformation EXISTS and is not an ansatz. CAUTION ON STRENGTH: the match is of PROJECTIVE normal forms, so what is established is that C's projectivisation is that of the family member at (p,q,t) - equality up to a rank-1 twist - in the same sense in which B and C are projectively equivalent. This is the reason the label is STRUCTURAL and not PROVEN.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "flow_regularity.py", "output_hash": "cd6657bbabf51e226e32de80324863227971cb9371f9c2e949a76db5300a4760", "review": "self", "review_note": "the pre-registered step-3(b) monodromy/Stokes falsifier at 30 digits was NOT run; this claim does not rest on it and does not stand in for it."}
{"claim_id": "S16-15", "task_id": "S16-STEP3B", "claim": "NOT ESTABLISHED: the pre-registered step-3(b) falsifier was NOT run. It requires integrating PV from (t_0,q,p) to t_0 + epsilon for two values of epsilon, rebuilding the linear system, and computing monodromy AND STOKES data agreeing with C's to at least 30 digits. Computing Stokes data for an irregular rank-2 system at that precision is a separate undertaking beyond this budget. The threshold in PREREG.md is left UNCHANGED for whenever it is run. What was done instead, and is reported as supplementary rather than as the falsifier, is the regularity check of the vector field (4.4) at the point.", "label": "CONJECTURED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "flow_regularity.py", "output_hash": "cd6657bbabf51e226e32de80324863227971cb9371f9c2e949a76db5300a4760", "review": "self", "review_note": "recorded as a gap; no threshold was weakened to close it."}
{"claim_id": "S16-16", "task_id": "S16-C3", "claim": "CONSEQUENCE FOR C3. The 'single fibre' concern - that System C sits at one fixed time t with no deformation written down - is, on this framework, a matter of PRESENTATION rather than a defect, because t is an invariant of the configuration (S16-04) and every point of M lies on a leaf (S16-03, S16-14). This does NOT license changing C3's wording in the companion v1.3 notice, which is an operator decision and is out of scope for this analysis-only session; no notice or conjecture file was edited.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": null, "output_hash": "cd6657bbabf51e226e32de80324863227971cb9371f9c2e949a76db5300a4760", "review": "self", "review_note": "consequence of S16-03, S16-04 and S16-14; flagged for the operator, not applied."}
{"claim_id": "S16-17", "task_id": "S16-METHOD", "claim": "P0 AMENDMENT PROPOSED, alongside the existing OCR rule: before a page image is used as evidence it must be confirmed to have RENDERED. The view tool accepts one image per message; two calls in a single message returned 'maximum number of images (1)' and displayed nothing, and reasoning had begun from page content that had never been seen. Caught and stopped; each page was then re-read alone in its own message. Rule: one image per message, and confirm it displayed before quoting it.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": null, "output_hash": "07356a233e946cb2a78678950aab34383fa02716391a2de3ad545fb3fa0ae8c3", "review": "self", "review_note": "method finding from this session; same family as S16-11."}
